From: Elevator HMI meta-hmi-platform
Subject: [PATCH] drm: panel: jadard — LMT101 VENDOR-CLOCK-MATCH (420 + Q1 20ms)

Sync the LMT101 path to LCD Mall vendor truth (email thread 11 May / 5 Jun /
13 Jun 2026):

1. PLL_CLOCK=420 (vendor init file) + 5 Jun "MIPI rate mismatch": drop
   MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST for all LMT101 enable sequences so the Rockchip
   dw-mipi-dsi host runs the lane rate at the mode-derived 70 MHz x 24 / 4 =
   420 Mbps instead of the 10/9 burst-margin 468 Mbps. Legacy cz101b4001
   (non-LMT101) keeps burst.
2. Vendor Q1 reset diagram: XRES low pulse width is 20 ms (not the init-file
   10 ms). This matches the sequence the customer reported to the FAE
   ("power on, 10 ms, XRES low 20 ms, XRES high, 120 ms") which the vendor
   confirmed lights the panel on their fixture.

Sentinel: jadard: VENDOR-CLOCK-MATCH

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
@@ -342,7 +342,7 @@ static int jadard_prepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 
 	if (jadard->reset) {
 		/*
-		 * Vendor Q1 (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW): XRES high 5 ms → low 10 ms → high 120 ms.
+		 * Vendor Q1 (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW): XRES high 5 ms → low 20 ms → high 120 ms.
 		 * gpiod 0 = inactive = pad high; gpiod 1 = active = pad low.
 		 */
 		gpiod_set_value(jadard->reset, 0);
@@ -350,7 +350,7 @@ static int jadard_prepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 
 		dev_info(panel->dev, "jadard: XRES assert\n");
 		gpiod_set_value(jadard->reset, 1);
-		msleep(10);
+		msleep(20); /* vendor Q1: 20 ms XRES low pulse width */
 
 		dev_info(panel->dev, "jadard: XRES release\n");
 		gpiod_set_value(jadard->reset, 0);
@@ -885,8 +885,8 @@ static int jadard_dsi_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 
 	desc = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
 	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO | MIPI_DSI_MODE_NO_EOT_PACKET;
-	if (desc->enable_seq == JADARD_ENABLE_SEQ_LMT101_FAE_BIST)
-		dev_info(dev, "jadard: FAE BIST path — VIDEO without BURST\n");
+	if (jadard_is_lmt101_enable_seq(desc->enable_seq))
+		dev_info(dev, "jadard: VENDOR-CLOCK-MATCH — VIDEO non-burst (PLL_CLOCK=420)\n");
 	else
 		dsi->mode_flags |= MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST;
 	dsi->format = desc->format;
